WEBVTT

00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:08.800
"AUGUST 11, 2095"

00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:08.800
"NINE SCHOOLS COMPETITION - DAY NINE"

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:10.340
"AUGUST 11, 2095"
"NINE SCHOOLS COMPETITION - DAY NINE"

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:10.340
In this weather...

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:16.010
it'll be easier to see the holograms in midair
during your Mirage Bat Final, Miyuki.

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:17.890
How lucky is that?

00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:22.850
Ms. Kobayakawa's playing, too,
so I don't think Miyuki's nervous at all.

00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:24.640
That's not true.

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:29.730
It's a lot of pressure just knowing I'm filling
in for First High's ace, Ms. Watanabe.

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:32.570
But you're going to be just fine, Miyuki!

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:35.030
After all, you have Tatsuya on your side!

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:39.160
Oh, that... Well, of course that's true, but...

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:45.500
There are only two days left
until the Nine Schools Competition is over.

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:48.960
Today's Mirage Bat
and tomorrow's Monolith Code...

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:51.340
If we win either one,

00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:54.170
it will seal First High's overall victory.

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:57.340
You don't have to worry about the school.

00:00:57.340 --> 00:01:00.220
Just focus on your match.

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:04.350
Thanks, Shizuku,
but I can't afford to do that.

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:05.230
What?

00:01:05.230 --> 00:01:08.520
We were able to get this far,
thanks to you and Honoka

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:13.440
and all the efforts of the First High team.

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:16.990
So, I have to live up to all that
in my own match.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:25.160
All grades will be competing
in the Mirage Bat Official Event.

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:26.750
Among the players...

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:38.720
Isshiki, I have no intention of losing, either!

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:42.760
I'm going to go all out
to lead First High to victory!

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:47.140
Yes. You don't have to tell me.

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:48.730
Goodbye.

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:53.860
That must be hard.

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:55.650
Having all those expectations to fulfill.

00:01:55.650 --> 00:01:58.240
Ms. Mizuo...

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:00.160
That was from the Isshiki Family, right?

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:02.030
I can never hide anything from you.

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:04.950
Well, we've known each other long enough.

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:07.500
They see Ichijo's loss yesterday

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:13.590
as a prime chance to show
our clout as another "One" family.

00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:17.220
A power struggle between clans
at a time like this?

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:22.930
The Nine Schools Competition is such a breeze
that you can win it with that on your mind.

00:02:22.930 --> 00:02:27.810
I feel terrible for my mother,
who came to Japan with so many dreams.

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:35.320
But that's precisely why I want to win.

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:38.240
Both for my mother's sake...

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:42.160
and above all, for my own sake!

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:43.740
I see.

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:46.290
Then, just as we promised...

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:50.540
The Mirage Bat Official Event will end...

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:52.670
with our one-two finish!

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:36.150
Mirage Bat Official Event,
First Match is about to begin!

00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:40.070
Be sure to feast your eyes
on each player's elaborate costume!

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:42.900
All right, I'm off!

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:46.530
Good luck, Ms. Kobayakawa!

00:04:46.530 --> 00:04:47.700
Just leave it to me!

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:51.370
Try to take the pressure off Shiba, Keiko!

00:04:51.370 --> 00:04:53.500
Roger that!

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:56.250
Her CAD's been adjusted to perfection...

00:04:56.250 --> 00:04:58.460
and Keiko's in great shape!

00:04:58.460 --> 00:05:00.840
She'll make it through
the qualifying round for sure!

00:05:14.350 --> 00:05:16.310
"QUALIFYING ROUND - FIRST MATCH:
KEIKO KOBAYAKAWA, CHIHIRO HASEGAWA,
ERIKA MUKAIYA, NATSUMI TOZAWA"

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:18.020
All right!

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:20.270
Just keep that up, Kobayakawa!

00:05:23.490 --> 00:05:27.240
Movement Spell.
I'm going to decelerate and get to that pole.

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:29.660
Keiko!

00:05:41.170 --> 00:05:43.210
Keiko, stay with me!

00:05:43.210 --> 00:05:47.680
Keiko! Why? Come on, Keiko!

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:49.390
Brother, this...

00:05:49.390 --> 00:05:50.720
I know.

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:53.560
Is that you, Mizuki?

00:05:57.190 --> 00:05:57.980
"FIRST HIGH SCHOOL"

00:05:57.980 --> 00:06:01.230
"FIRST HIGH SCHOOL"

00:05:57.980 --> 00:06:01.230
Ms. Kobayakawa had to forfeit the match?

00:06:01.230 --> 00:06:02.730
What was the cause of the accident?

00:06:02.730 --> 00:06:07.700
My brother suspects that it's her CAD.
That it must've been tampered with somehow.

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:12.030
No way! Not when the Tournament Committee
checked it before the match!

00:06:12.030 --> 00:06:14.490
Would they really go that far?

00:06:14.490 --> 00:06:17.410
My brother's down there now,
trying to find out.

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:19.710
W-We have a problem!

00:06:19.710 --> 00:06:21.080
It's Tatsuya!

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:22.380
"ADMINISTRATION DEPARTMENT"

00:06:22.380 --> 00:06:24.460
"ADMINISTRATION DEPARTMENT"

00:06:22.380 --> 00:06:24.460
You've really underestimated me.

00:06:26.170 --> 00:06:29.180
What did you try to inject
into Miyuki's CAD?

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:32.800
Hey, did you hear...

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:37.640
about that engineer from First High
going berserk in the Committee's tent?

00:06:37.640 --> 00:06:41.560
--I heard he really did
a number on the official.
--Are you serious?

00:06:41.560 --> 00:06:44.110
He vented his anger on him?
That's scary.

00:06:44.110 --> 00:06:48.530
You're wrong. My brother would never
get angry over something like that.

00:06:48.530 --> 00:06:49.700
I just know it.

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:50.860
Miyuki!

00:06:54.410 --> 00:06:56.910
I'm sorry I made you worry.

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:05.210
You only ever get angry on my account,
and you always take all the criticism for that.

00:07:05.210 --> 00:07:08.510
Really! Brother, you're such a fool!

00:07:08.510 --> 00:07:10.630
U-Um...

00:07:10.630 --> 00:07:15.140
"Doing such a thing on my account!"

00:07:15.140 --> 00:07:18.270
"I'm sorry, Miyuki, I made you worry."

00:07:18.270 --> 00:07:21.480
President! Ms. Watanabe!

00:07:24.150 --> 00:07:28.110
I'm told one of our students went on a rampage,
and what did it turn out to be?

00:07:28.110 --> 00:07:31.950
Just a big brother with a hard-core
sister complex who went berserk as usual

00:07:31.950 --> 00:07:34.910
because someone messed
with his precious little sister!

00:07:34.910 --> 00:07:36.870
For his little sister.

00:07:36.870 --> 00:07:38.450
Sister complex.

00:07:38.450 --> 00:07:40.080
--He's that kind of guy...
--There's a slight change in the air,
so maybe this is okay.

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:43.000
--That's scary in whole different way!
--There's a slight change in the air,
so maybe this is okay.

00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:47.960
"THIRD HIGH SCHOOL"

00:07:48.250 --> 00:07:50.630
Something happened
to another First High player?

00:07:50.630 --> 00:07:53.180
Airi, do you think this is...

00:07:53.180 --> 00:07:55.720
That sabotage operation
we've been talking about.

00:07:55.720 --> 00:08:00.390
Now what, forsooth, could their purpose be?
Going after First High exclusively!

00:08:00.390 --> 00:08:02.810
I wonder if Ms. Shiba's all right.

00:08:02.810 --> 00:08:04.310
Thanks for waiting.

00:08:04.310 --> 00:08:05.730
We're all set now.

00:08:05.730 --> 00:08:09.440
So, you're going with a straightforward
attack again this time.

00:08:09.440 --> 00:08:15.660
Right. Just like you, I'm going to try to win
using my well-trained Jump Spell.

00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:17.990
I'm sure you're going to be just fine!

00:08:23.290 --> 00:08:27.710
Who would've thought a tournament official
would be the one tampering with that CAD?

00:08:27.710 --> 00:08:33.260
If it hadn't been for Shibata's eyes
and Tatsuya's checkup, we could've been buried.

00:08:33.260 --> 00:08:36.800
I sure didn't do
Shiba's little sister any favors.

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:38.890
Not only does she have to take my place,

00:08:38.890 --> 00:08:42.060
but now, she also has the destiny
of First High on her shoulders.

00:08:42.060 --> 00:08:44.480
Hey, that doesn't worry me one bit.

00:08:44.480 --> 00:08:45.730
Huh?

00:08:45.730 --> 00:08:51.110
After all, Shiba will eventually carry
First High on her shoulders.

00:08:51.110 --> 00:08:53.360
I wonder what kind of costume
Miyuki will be wearing!

00:08:53.360 --> 00:08:57.160
--She said it was ordinary.
--No way is it going to be ordinary!

00:08:57.160 --> 00:09:02.620
I mean, she said it would be orthodox
for Pillars Break, and look what she wore.

00:09:02.620 --> 00:09:06.710
Mirage Bat Second Match!
The players are now entering!

00:09:15.550 --> 00:09:17.090
Miyuki's so gorgeous!

00:09:17.090 --> 00:09:18.760
That's our Miyuki!

00:09:18.760 --> 00:09:23.730
It's not her costume that's extraordinary!
It's the model herself, huh?

00:09:23.730 --> 00:09:26.100
That's the girl who won Pillars Break.

00:09:26.100 --> 00:09:30.900
Sure, she's good at Oscillation Magic,
but I can hold my own with Jump Spells!

00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:34.570
We just can't lose as third years, can we?

00:09:36.570 --> 00:09:37.530
"QUALIFYING ROUND - SECOND MATCH"

00:09:44.830 --> 00:09:45.870
So fast.

00:09:48.670 --> 00:09:49.750
But...

00:09:56.930 --> 00:09:58.550
Not bad.

00:09:58.550 --> 00:10:00.550
Shiba is something else, isn't she?

00:10:00.550 --> 00:10:04.560
A first year, holding her own
against Ms. Mizuo?

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:07.270
The other students
are breathing down her neck!

00:10:07.270 --> 00:10:09.980
The final's on a different level, yes?

00:10:11.060 --> 00:10:12.480
What's wrong?

00:10:15.320 --> 00:10:17.400
The second period is now over.

00:10:17.860 --> 00:10:20.620
"QUALIFYING ROUND - SECOND MATCH:
MIYUKI SHIBA, SAHO MIZUO,
AYUMI KAMINO, RINA AKASAKA"

00:10:21.410 --> 00:10:25.620
Just what you'd expect of the Nine Schools
Competition. Every single player is formidable.

00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:28.210
But I can't afford to lose.

00:10:28.210 --> 00:10:29.540
I don't want to lose!

00:10:30.330 --> 00:10:31.630
Brother...

00:10:33.550 --> 00:10:35.460
Is it okay if I use that?

00:10:38.010 --> 00:10:39.510
Go ahead.

00:10:39.510 --> 00:10:42.010
You can do anything you want.

00:10:43.970 --> 00:10:46.220
Go on and give it your all, Miyuki.

00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:49.310
Right!

00:10:49.310 --> 00:10:51.190
She'll finally use it.

00:10:51.190 --> 00:10:52.230
Huh?

00:10:52.230 --> 00:10:55.150
The spell that I couldn't master myself.

00:11:06.700 --> 00:11:09.330
Please watch me, Brother.

00:11:10.420 --> 00:11:11.460
I will fly!

00:11:15.800 --> 00:11:16.840
Huh?

00:11:18.880 --> 00:11:20.260
Th-That's...

00:11:23.300 --> 00:11:24.640
No way!

00:11:24.640 --> 00:11:26.180
Flying Magic?

00:11:47.240 --> 00:11:50.500
Sh-She's flying! She's really flying!

00:11:50.500 --> 00:11:55.170
Flying Magic. With no success stories,
it's always been considered impossible.

00:11:55.170 --> 00:11:59.010
Taurus Silver just announced it
last month, right?

00:11:59.010 --> 00:12:02.050
Tatsuya suggested
that Honoka and I try it, too,

00:12:02.050 --> 00:12:05.010
but there wasn't enough time
to master it.

00:12:05.010 --> 00:12:09.520
Miyuki can already fly at will.
Miyuki's amazing, after all!

00:12:10.140 --> 00:12:16.940
That spell was only just announced,
but her magic breathing is quite stable, yes?

00:12:16.940 --> 00:12:19.610
She's made it completely her own.

00:12:30.870 --> 00:12:36.040
It's no good! I can't get there
with my Jump Spell! But...

00:12:36.040 --> 00:12:38.130
I can't just go down without a fight!

00:12:44.090 --> 00:12:45.300
Airi...

00:12:45.510 --> 00:12:47.140
"QUALIFYING ROUND - SECOND MATCH:
MIYUKI SHIBA, SAHO MIZUO,
AYUMI KAMINO, RINA AKASAKA"

00:12:47.140 --> 00:12:52.180
Winner of the second match,
First High School's Miyuki Shiba!

00:13:07.620 --> 00:13:09.200
Brother!

00:13:13.660 --> 00:13:16.370
Along with her overwhelming magic power...

00:13:16.370 --> 00:13:20.550
to think she's even mastered Flying Magic...
Troublesome, yes?

00:13:20.550 --> 00:13:22.670
I admit that I was taken aback,

00:13:22.670 --> 00:13:28.680
but it's not as if we can't reach the holograms
after they've appeared using Jump Spells.

00:13:29.930 --> 00:13:32.060
No need to worry, Shiori.

00:13:34.390 --> 00:13:38.610
We're going to defeat her
using our collective skills.

00:13:38.610 --> 00:13:42.360
I can't just stand here
getting a pep talk.

00:13:42.360 --> 00:13:45.360
I have to help Airi out more.

00:13:45.360 --> 00:13:47.950
Right! Give it your all, Shiori!

00:13:49.070 --> 00:13:51.080
Ms. Mizuo...

00:13:51.080 --> 00:13:55.080
I'm sorry. For breaking our promise.

00:13:55.080 --> 00:13:57.210
I feel so pathetic.

00:13:57.210 --> 00:14:02.000
No. Watching your battle
provided me with numerous hints.

00:14:13.310 --> 00:14:18.850
Compared to Shiba's Flying Magic,
I can't stay in the air anywhere near as long.

00:14:35.620 --> 00:14:37.250
S-So fast!

00:14:37.250 --> 00:14:38.620
No way!

00:14:38.620 --> 00:14:42.380
I'm going to surpass her flying speed
with my jump speed!

00:14:42.670 --> 00:14:44.340
"QUALIFYING ROUND - SIXTH MATCH:
AIRI ISSHIKI, YOKO MATSUI"

00:14:44.340 --> 00:14:45.920
Game over!

00:14:45.920 --> 00:14:50.180
Winner, Third High School's Airi Isshiki!

00:14:59.230 --> 00:15:03.940
Thank goodness. I was able
to present my brother with a win.

00:15:03.940 --> 00:15:08.240
That Flying Magic
is dear to my brother's heart.

00:15:08.240 --> 00:15:14.200
I'm so thrilled that I was able
to make its unveiling a success!

00:15:14.200 --> 00:15:17.290
"Our CAD," did you say?

00:15:17.290 --> 00:15:19.080
Forgive us.

00:15:19.080 --> 00:15:23.130
We're fielding questions
from the other schools about Flying Magic.

00:15:23.130 --> 00:15:25.550
But it's a model that's completely
within regulations,

00:15:25.550 --> 00:15:28.590
and the technology
has already been announced.

00:15:28.590 --> 00:15:31.050
We're well aware of that.

00:15:31.050 --> 00:15:34.180
There are tournament officials here.

00:15:34.180 --> 00:15:38.270
I admit I don't blame them
for being dubious.

00:15:38.270 --> 00:15:41.900
When they see the streamlined design
of that CAD and the magic sequences,

00:15:41.900 --> 00:15:44.650
perhaps they'll actually be stunned!

00:15:49.940 --> 00:15:53.490
Our target in the second match
made it to the final.

00:15:53.490 --> 00:15:56.620
Not only that,
but by a huge margin, too!

00:15:56.620 --> 00:15:59.370
They've gotten wise
to our CAD tampering, too!

00:15:59.370 --> 00:16:04.790
At this rate, First High's overall victory
will be sealed today!

00:16:04.790 --> 00:16:07.710
Now that it's come to this,
we have to go to our last resort.

00:16:07.710 --> 00:16:09.630
Right.

00:16:09.630 --> 00:16:12.180
We're going to shut down
the Nine Schools Competition!

00:16:12.180 --> 00:16:19.100
Using a Generator to indiscriminately kill
a hundred or so of the audience should suffice.

00:16:19.100 --> 00:16:23.190
All right, I'm removing the limiter.

00:16:36.700 --> 00:16:39.040
Right.

00:16:39.040 --> 00:16:41.290
Understood. Goodbye.

00:16:41.290 --> 00:16:43.670
Brother, is something wrong?

00:16:43.670 --> 00:16:45.290
No, it's nothing.

00:16:45.290 --> 00:16:48.170
There's still time before the final.

00:16:48.170 --> 00:16:49.920
You should get some rest now.

00:16:49.920 --> 00:16:50.920
Okay.

00:16:50.920 --> 00:16:54.090
If there's something you want me
to do for you, let me know.

00:16:54.090 --> 00:16:55.390
Whatever you want.

00:16:55.390 --> 00:16:56.590
What?

00:16:56.590 --> 00:16:58.890
"Whatever I want," did you say?

00:17:13.650 --> 00:17:14.700
Miyuki?

00:17:15.990 --> 00:17:18.240
U-Um...

00:17:18.240 --> 00:17:20.290
In that case...

00:17:20.290 --> 00:17:25.170
I was wondering if you could stay
by my side until I fall asleep.

00:17:26.750 --> 00:17:29.880
You really are a baby, Miyuki.

00:17:29.880 --> 00:17:35.760
I-Is that wrong?
I want to be spoiled, Brother!

00:17:35.760 --> 00:17:36.720
Fine, then.

00:17:36.720 --> 00:17:38.010
Really?

00:17:38.010 --> 00:17:41.100
I can't sing you a lullaby, though.

00:17:41.100 --> 00:17:43.480
Well, that is a pity.

00:17:53.230 --> 00:17:58.990
Whoever they may be,
I'll exterminate anyone who may harm you.

00:17:58.990 --> 00:18:02.290
I will never waver when it comes to that.

00:18:02.290 --> 00:18:04.160
It's my highest priority.

00:18:06.210 --> 00:18:08.170
Brother...

00:18:14.380 --> 00:18:16.380
I'm flying, Brother!

00:18:17.880 --> 00:18:21.300
I can use Flying Magic, too!

00:18:21.720 --> 00:18:25.890
This is a special spell
that my brother created.

00:18:27.140 --> 00:18:32.230
My brother should be the one
receiving all of the glory and praise.

00:18:32.230 --> 00:18:33.820
And yet...

00:18:36.860 --> 00:18:43.200
The yoke known as the Yotsuba Clan keeps
taking away my brother's glory and shackles him.

00:18:43.200 --> 00:18:47.460
I hate myself for not being able
to do anything, for being so helpless!

00:18:47.460 --> 00:18:48.750
But...

00:18:50.750 --> 00:18:59.510
But I'm using my powers
so that I can set him free one day.

00:19:02.100 --> 00:19:04.560
All of the players will be using Flying Magic?

00:19:04.560 --> 00:19:09.730
Yes. The tournament staff has disclosed
First High's CAD information.

00:19:09.730 --> 00:19:14.610
It's likely that all of the schools
will be using Flying Magic in the final.

00:19:14.610 --> 00:19:18.570
If it were only Shiba,
I'm confident that I could take her on.

00:19:18.570 --> 00:19:21.160
But if everyone's going to be using it...

00:19:22.370 --> 00:19:26.120
We can't beat First High
if all we can do is merely fly.

00:19:26.120 --> 00:19:31.250
She is already in her element
when she uses Flying Magic.

00:19:31.250 --> 00:19:34.090
This isn't something
that superficial knowledge can cure.

00:19:35.210 --> 00:19:37.380
To be honest, I'm at a loss.

00:19:37.380 --> 00:19:40.010
There's also the risk that unfamiliar
magic could cause us to self-destruct.

00:19:40.010 --> 00:19:42.220
--Then--
--Still!

00:19:43.010 --> 00:19:47.220
I can't defeat Shiba unless I go all out.

00:19:47.220 --> 00:19:50.190
That's why I want to bet on it!

00:19:50.190 --> 00:19:52.150
On my own potential!

00:19:53.440 --> 00:19:56.400
And I'm going to need your help
toward that end.

00:19:56.400 --> 00:19:59.490
Will you make the adjustments
for Flying Magic?

00:19:59.490 --> 00:20:04.160
Y-Yes. I'll do everything I can, but...

00:20:04.160 --> 00:20:07.950
Shiori, I believe in your skills.

00:20:11.960 --> 00:20:13.210
Fine, then.

00:20:16.800 --> 00:20:19.590
I have one other idea, too.

00:20:25.220 --> 00:20:26.850
Thank you for waiting!

00:20:26.850 --> 00:20:30.430
It's time for the
Mirage Bat Official Event Final!

00:20:30.430 --> 00:20:34.270
The star-studded skies await
the arrival of the players!

00:20:34.270 --> 00:20:38.730
In the qualifying rounds, it was Ms. Shiba's
use of Flying Magic that had everyone buzzing,

00:20:38.730 --> 00:20:42.820
but all of the players turned in
splendid performances!

00:20:42.820 --> 00:20:46.070
Now, who will emerge victorious?

00:20:47.200 --> 00:20:49.580
I'm not in the least bit worried!

00:20:49.580 --> 00:20:52.660
Where there's a will,
there's a way!

00:20:52.660 --> 00:20:54.960
You're my pride and joy.

00:20:54.960 --> 00:20:56.790
The pride and joy of Third High!

00:20:56.790 --> 00:20:58.500
Thank you very much.

00:20:58.500 --> 00:20:59.550
Airi...

00:21:02.220 --> 00:21:04.380
I believe in you.

00:21:06.090 --> 00:21:07.470
Now then...

00:21:11.680 --> 00:21:13.020
I'll be off!

00:21:17.860 --> 00:21:19.150
Thank you for waiting.

00:21:19.150 --> 00:21:20.900
That really becomes you.

00:21:20.900 --> 00:21:24.570
If Mirage Bat had artistic scores,
you'd get a perfect 10.

00:21:24.570 --> 00:21:26.870
Brother, please!

00:21:26.870 --> 00:21:28.780
You look well.

00:21:28.780 --> 00:21:35.420
Yes. I have good energy, as well,
so I'd like to start off with Flying Magic.

00:21:35.420 --> 00:21:37.040
Fine.

00:21:37.040 --> 00:21:38.920
Go fly to your heart's content.

00:21:40.750 --> 00:21:42.550
Yes, Brother!
